IMPORT prelude

-- ============================================================
-- Fact schema, copied verbatim from inputs/schema.md, so this
-- file is self-contained. No claim data lives here.
-- ============================================================

§ `Fact schema`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER
      `confined in us hospital`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `continuous confinement days`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `claim made setting out basis`               IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Supporting helpers (pre-defined -- called below, never redefined)`

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

-- ============================================================
-- Section 1 -- POLICY IN EFFECT AND CONDITIONS
-- ============================================================

§ `1. Policy in effect and conditions`

§§ `1.1(1)(2)(4) and 1.2 -- signed, premium paid, not cancelled`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the policy is in effect` claim MEANS
       claim's `agreement signed`
   AND `the premium has been paid` claim
   AND `condition 1.3 is pending or satisfied` claim
   AND NOT (`fraud or misrepresentation has occurred` claim)
   AND claim's `hospitalization month` AT MOST claim's `policy term months`

-- 1.1(2): "the applicable premium ... has been paid" -- paid, and paid
-- by the time of the hospitalization it is meant to cover.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the premium has been paid` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `premium paid month`
      WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
      WHEN JUST p  THEN p AT MOST claim's `hospitalization month`

-- 1.2: cancellation for "fraud, or any misrepresentation or material
-- withholding of any information". The schema gives one field for
-- misrepresentation/withholding, so `misrepresentation month` stands
-- for both (see NOTES.md).
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fraud or misrepresentation has occurred` claim MEANS
       isJust (claim's `fraud month`)
   OR  isJust (claim's `misrepresentation month`)

§§ `1.3 -- wellness visit and written confirmation`

-- 1.1(3): "the condition set out in Section 1.3 is still pending or
-- has been satisfied in a timely fashion" -- evaluated as of the
-- hospitalization. Before the outer (7-month) deadline the condition
-- has simply not come due yet; from that point on it must actually
-- have been met.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 is pending or satisfied` claim MEANS
       claim's `hospitalization month` LESS THAN 7
   OR  `condition 1.3 is satisfied` claim

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 is satisfied` claim MEANS
       `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
   AND claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`
   AND `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7

-- ============================================================
-- Section 2 -- BENEFITS
-- ============================================================

§ `2. Benefits`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the benefit conditions of section 2 are met` claim MEANS
       `hospitalization is of a covered kind` claim
   AND claim's `confined in us hospital`
   AND `there was continuous confinement` claim

-- 2.1: "as a result of sickness or accidental Injury".
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization is of a covered kind` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `hospitalization ground`
      WHEN Sickness            THEN TRUE
      WHEN `Accidental injury` THEN TRUE
      WHEN Neither              THEN FALSE

-- 2.2: "payable for each (24 hour) day of continuous confinement".
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`there was continuous confinement` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `continuous confinement days`
      WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
      WHEN JUST d  THEN d GREATER THAN 0

-- 2.3's own requirement ("a claim must be made ... setting out the
-- basis") is `claim`'s `claim made setting out basis` field, used
-- directly in `covered` below; the rest of 2.3 ("no exclusion or
-- cancellation") is the `an exclusion applies` and
-- `the policy is in effect` checks already present elsewhere.

-- ============================================================
-- Section 3 -- GENERAL EXCLUSIONS
-- ============================================================

§ `3. General exclusions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an exclusion applies` claim MEANS
       `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`
   OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

-- ============================================================
-- Section 4 -- GENERAL CONDITIONS
-- ============================================================

§ `4. General conditions`

§§ `4.2 -- arbitration and the sixty-day proof-of-claim wait`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the arbitration and proof-of-claim conditions are met` claim MEANS
       `the dispute condition is met` claim
   AND `recovery was not sought prematurely` claim

-- "the issuance of a valid arbitration award shall also be a
-- condition precedent to our liability" -- only bites when a dispute
-- has in fact arisen.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dispute condition is met` claim MEANS
    IF   claim's `dispute arisen`
    THEN     `arbitration was timely commenced` claim
         AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`
    ELSE TRUE

-- "such arbitration to be commenced within three (3) months from the
-- day such parties are unable to settle the dispute".
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration was timely commenced` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `unable to settle month`
      WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
      WHEN JUST m  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (m PLUS 3)

-- "In no case shall You seek to recover ... before the expiration of
-- sixty (60) days after written proof of claim has been submitted".
-- The schema's time unit is months; 60 days is taken as 2 months
-- (see NOTES.md).
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery was not sought prematurely` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
      WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
      WHEN JUST r  THEN CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
          WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
          WHEN JUST w  THEN r AT LEAST (w PLUS 2)

-- ============================================================
-- Top-level decision
-- ============================================================

§ `Coverage decision`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
covered claim MEANS
       `the policy is in effect` claim
   AND `the benefit conditions of section 2 are met` claim
   AND claim's `claim made setting out basis`
   AND NOT (`an exclusion applies` claim)
   AND `the arbitration and proof-of-claim conditions are met` claim
